</style></head> <body> <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a> <nav class="nav"> <div class="nav-inner"> <a href="/" class="nav-logo">AI<span>ToolPick</span></a> <button class="nav-toggle" aria-label="Toggle menu" id="nav-toggle">&#9776;</button> <ul class="nav-links" id="nav-links"> <li><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/">Compare</a></li> <li><a href="/top/">Top 10</a></li> <li><a href="/best-for/">Best For</a></li> <li><a href="/stacks/">Stacks</a></li> <li><a href="/free/">Free</a></li> <li><a href="/quiz/">Quiz</a></li> <li><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></li> </ul> <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" title="Toggle dark mode"> <span id="theme-icon">&#9728;&#65039;</span> </button> </div> </nav> <main id="main-content">  <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Plans, AI Credits, and What Changed","description":"GitHub Copilot pricing explained — Free, Pro, Pro+, Business plans with the new usage-based billing system launching June 2026.","datePublished":"2026-05-02T00:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-05-02T00:00:00.000Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AIToolPick","url":"https://aitoolpick.org"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AIToolPick","url":"https://aitoolpick.org"},"image":"https://aitoolpick.org/thumbs/github-copilot-pricing-2026.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://aitoolpick.org/blog/github-copilot-pricing-2026/"}}</script> <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://aitoolpick.org"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Blog","item":"https://aitoolpick.org/blog/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Plans, AI Credits, and What Changed","item":"https://aitoolpick.org/blog/github-copilot-pricing-2026/"}]}</script> <article class="article"> <!-- Breadcrumb navigation --> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <ol> <li><a href="/">Home</a></li> <li><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></li> <li aria-current="page">GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Plans, AI Credits, and What ...</li> </ol> </nav> <header class="article-header"> <p class="article-date">
Published May 2, 2026  </p> <h1>GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Plans, AI Credits, and What Changed</h1> <div class="article-tags"> <a href="/blog/tag/github-copilot/" class="card-tag">github-copilot</a><a href="/blog/tag/ai-coding/" class="card-tag">ai-coding</a><a href="/blog/tag/pricing/" class="card-tag">pricing</a> </div> </header> <img class="article-hero" src="/thumbs/github-copilot-pricing-2026.jpg" alt="GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Plans, AI Credits, and What Changed"> <!-- AdSense: article top（収益化テスト 2026-09-03〜。スロットはexpo2025と共用、専用ユニット発行後に差し替え） --> <div class="ad-unit ad-unit-top"> <span class="ad-label">Advertisement</span> <ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block" data-ad-client="ca-pub-4052959814764437" data-ad-slot="7388501974" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins> <script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script> </div> <div class="article-content">  <p>GitHub Copilot is the most widely used <a href="/category/ai-coding/">AI coding</a> assistant, and its pricing is about to change significantly. Starting June 1, 2026, Copilot moves from request-based billing to a usage-based credit system. Here’s what you need to know.</p>
<h2 id="current-plans-before-june-2026">Current Plans (Before June 2026)</h2>



































<table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>Included</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Free</strong></td><td>$0</td><td>2,000 completions + 50 chat requests/month</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pro</strong></td><td>$10/mo</td><td>Unlimited completions + premium requests</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pro+</strong></td><td>$39/mo</td><td>Everything in Pro + more premium requests</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong></td><td>$19/user/mo</td><td>Team management + policy controls</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Enterprise</strong></td><td>$39/user/mo</td><td>Everything + IP indemnity</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="what-changes-on-june-1-2026">What Changes on June 1, 2026</h2>
<p>GitHub is replacing “premium requests” with <strong>AI Credits</strong>. The plan prices stay the same, but what you get is measured differently.</p>
<h3 id="how-ai-credits-work">How AI Credits Work</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>1 AI credit = $0.01 USD</strong></li>
<li>Each plan includes monthly credits equal to its price: Pro gets $10 in credits, Business gets $19 per user</li>
<li>Credits are consumed based on the AI model used and tokens processed</li>
<li><strong>Code completions remain unlimited</strong> on all paid plans — they don’t use credits</li>
<li><strong>Next Edit Suggestions remain unlimited</strong> on paid plans</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="what-uses-credits">What Uses Credits</h3>
<ul>
<li>Chat messages (in editor, on GitHub.com, in CLI)</li>
<li>Copilot Edits (multi-file editing)</li>
<li>Agent mode sessions</li>
<li>Using premium models (<a href="/tools/claude/">Claude</a> Sonnet, GPT-4o, etc.)</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="whats-still-freeunlimited">What’s Still Free/Unlimited</h3>
<ul>
<li>Code completions (Tab suggestions)</li>
<li>Next Edit Suggestions</li>
<li>Using the default model for completions</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="plan-by-plan-breakdown">Plan-by-Plan Breakdown</h2>
<h3 id="free-0month">Free ($0/month)</h3>
<p><a href="/tools/github-copilot-x/">GitHub Copilot</a> Free gives everyone a taste:</p>
<ul>
<li>2,000 code completions per month</li>
<li>50 chat requests per month (including Copilot Edits)</li>
<li>Limited model selection</li>
</ul>
<p>Good enough for students or light hobby use. Not viable for full-time development.</p>
<h3 id="pro-10month">Pro ($10/month)</h3>
<p>The standard individual plan:</p>
<ul>
<li>Unlimited code completions</li>
<li>$10 in monthly AI credits</li>
<li>Access to all available models</li>
<li>Copilot Chat, Edits, and Agent mode</li>
</ul>
<p>At $10/month, this is the cheapest paid AI coding assistant on the market — half the price of <a href="/blog/cursor-pricing-2026">Cursor Pro</a>.</p>
<h3 id="pro-39month">Pro+ ($39/month)</h3>
<p>For <a href="/best-for/developers/">developers</a> who need heavy chat and Agent usage:</p>
<ul>
<li>Everything in Pro</li>
<li>$39 in monthly AI credits (3.9x Pro)</li>
<li>Higher rate limits</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="business-19usermonth">Business ($19/user/month)</h3>
<p>Built for organizations:</p>
<ul>
<li>Everything in Pro for each seat</li>
<li>$19 in monthly AI credits per user</li>
<li>Organization-wide policy management</li>
<li>Audit logs</li>
<li>IP indemnity</li>
<li>Exclude specified files from Copilot</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="enterprise-39usermonth">Enterprise ($39/user/month)</h3>
<p>Everything in Business, plus:</p>
<ul>
<li>Fine-tuned models on your codebase</li>
<li>Extended AI credits per user</li>
<li>Priority support</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="migration-timeline">Migration Timeline</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Monthly Pro/Pro+ subscribers</strong>: Automatically move to usage-based billing on June 1, 2026</li>
<li><strong>Annual Pro/Pro+ subscribers</strong>: Stay on request-based billing until their current term expires</li>
<li><strong>Business/Enterprise</strong>: Transition managed by GitHub account teams</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="is-github-copilot-still-worth-it">Is GitHub Copilot Still Worth It?</h2>
<p>At $10/month, Copilot Pro remains the best value in AI coding tools. The credit system may feel limiting for heavy Agent users, but unlimited completions — which is what most developers use most — stay free on all paid plans.</p>
<p>The real question is whether $10 of credits is enough for your chat and editing needs. If you routinely use Agent mode and premium models, the $39 Pro+ plan or a competitor like <a href="/blog/cursor-review-2026">Cursor</a> may be more cost-effective.</p>
<h2 id="how-copilot-pricing-compares">How Copilot Pricing Compares</h2>





























<table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Base Paid Plan</th><th>Completions</th><th>Agent/Chat</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GitHub Copilot</strong></td><td>$10/mo</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Credit-based</td></tr><tr><td><strong><a href="/tools/cursor/">Cursor</a></strong></td><td>$20/mo</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Credit-based</td></tr><tr><td><strong><a href="/tools/windsurf/">Windsurf</a></strong></td><td>~$15/mo</td><td>Free all tiers</td><td>Quota-based</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>For a full comparison, read <a href="/blog/cursor-vs-github-copilot-2026">Cursor vs GitHub Copilot</a> or explore our <a href="/blog/best-ai-code-assistants-2026">best AI code assistants guide</a>.</p>  </div> <!-- AdSense: article bottom --> <div class="ad-unit ad-unit-bottom"> <span class="ad-label">Advertisement</span> <ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block" data-ad-client="ca-pub-4052959814764437" data-ad-slot="2555862179" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins> <script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script> </div> <!-- Source & update info --> <div class="article-meta-footer"> <p>Last reviewed and updated: May 2, 2026</p> <p>Pricing and feature information may change. Visit the official product website for the latest details.</p> </div> <!-- Related Articles --> <section class="related-articles"> <h2>Related Articles</h2> <div class="related-grid"> <a href="/blog/github-copilot-usage-based-billing-2026/" class="related-card"> <h3>GitHub Copilot Usage-Based Billing: Everything You Need to Know (June 2026)</h3> <p>GitHub Copilot is moving to AI Credits in June 2026. Here&#39;s what changes, what stays free, and how it affects your bill.</p> </a><a href="/blog/github-copilot-free-vs-paid-2026/" class="related-card"> <h3>GitHub Copilot Free vs Paid 2026: Is Pro Worth $10?</h3> <p>GitHub Copilot free vs Pro ($10/mo) compared — completion limits, chat requests, model access, and how June 2026 usage-b...</p> </a><a href="/blog/ai-coding-assistant-pricing-comparison-2026/" class="related-card"> <h3>AI Coding Assistant Pricing Comparison 2026: Every Tool&#39;s Real Cost</h3> <p>Compare AI coding assistant pricing in 2026 — Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, and Devin costs side...</p> </a><a href="/blog/cursor-vs-github-copilot-pricing-2026/" class="related-card"> <h3>Cursor vs GitHub Copilot Pricing 2026: Real Monthly Cost Compared</h3> <p>Cursor vs GitHub Copilot pricing in 2026 — $20 credit pool vs Copilot&#39;s new usage-based AI credits. Which AI coding tool...</p> </a> </div> </section> <!-- CTA --> <div class="cta-section"> <h2>Find the Best Tool for You</h2> <p>Compare features, pricing, and reviews to find the perfect tool for your workflow.</p> <a href="/alternatives/github-copilot/" class="btn-primary">See github-copilot alternatives &rarr;</a> </div> </article>  </main> <section class="newsletter-section" data-astro-cid-motrwrji> <div class="newsletter-inner" data-astro-cid-motrwrji> <h2 data-astro-cid-motrwrji>Stay ahead of AI — Weekly tool picks, straight to your inbox.</h2> <p data-astro-cid-motrwrji>Join thousands of professionals who get curated AI tool recommendations every week. No spam, unsubscribe anytime.</p> <form class="newsletter-form" action="https://formspree.io/f/placeholder" method="POST" data-astro-cid-motrwrji> <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required aria-label="Email address" data-astro-cid-motrwrji> <button type="submit" data-astro-cid-motrwrji>Subscribe</button> </form> </div> </section>  <footer class="footer"> <div class="footer-inner"> <div class="footer-brand"> <h3>AI<span>ToolPick</span></h3> <p>Helping you find the perfect tools for your workflow. Honest comparisons, no fluff.</p> <div class="footer-social"> <a href="https://x.com/AIToolPick" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Follow us on X (Twitter)">&#120143;</a> </div> </div> <div class="footer-col"> <h4>Compare</h4> <ul> <li><a href="/compare/">All Comparisons</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/notion-vs-clickup/">Notion vs ClickUp</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/chatgpt-vs-claude/">ChatGPT vs Claude</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/canva-vs-figma/">Canva vs Figma</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/cursor-vs-github-copilot/">Cursor vs Copilot</a></li> <li><a href="/compare/asana-vs-monday/">Asana vs Monday</a></li> </ul> </div> <div class="footer-col"> <h4>Best For</h4> <ul> <li><a href="/best-for/freelancers/">Freelancers</a